Hi Delin,

Unfortunately, the print.svm <https://github.com/cran/e1071/blob/master/R/svm.R#L521> function always returns NULL, so you won't be able to get what you want by looking at the return value of print(), it will always be NULL.'

Instead, the print() function will simply output the text you've circled as "B" to the ScriptEngine's standard output stream, which is by default sent to the process' standard output stream

I've added a section to our documentation on how to do this:
http://docs.renjin.org/en/latest/library/capture.html

You can redirect the output from R to a StringWriter this way:
StringWriter outputWriter = new StringWriter();
engine.getContext().setWriter(outputWriter);
engine.eval("print(svmfit)");

String output = outputWriter.toString();

// Reset output to console
engine.getContext().setWriter(new PrintWriter(System.out));

Hope this helps,
Alex

